@hidden
Feature: The G4 page says how the change works (hidden examples)

  Background:
    Given a GDD project in a git repository with the protected paths:
      """
      [protected]
      all = ["gdd/**", "bin/**"]
      builder_build = ["features/**", "tests/steps/**"]
      builder_test = ["src/**"]
      """
    And the zone map:
      """
      default = "yellow"

      [[zone]]
      color = "red"
      paths = ["src/storage/**"]
      reason = "Losing the user's drafts"
      """
    And the models:
      """
      [orchestrator]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "opus"

      [builder.yellow]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "sonnet"

      [builder.red]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "opus"

      [builder_test]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "sonnet"

      [reviewer]
      integration = "codex"
      model = "gpt-6"

      [families]
      "opus" = "anthropic"
      "sonnet" = "anthropic"
      "gpt" = "openai"
      """
    And the gate commands:
      """
      [g2]
      unit = "test -f src/app.txt"

      [g3]
      acceptance_full = "true"

      [release]
      simulated = true
      build = "true"
      deploy_pre = "true"
      tests_pre = "true"
      demo = ""
      promote = ""
      observe = ""
      rollback = ""
      """
    And the scenario "features/base.feature" with 1 scenarios
    And everything is committed on main
    And the Setup is done
    And the red zones are approved
    And the agents are fakes

  Scenario: The explanation ends at the next heading
    Given I run "gdd new-change c1 --title App --paths src/app.txt"
    And the change "c1" has the scenario "features/app.feature" on its branch
    And I am on the branch "change/c1"
    And I run "gdd gate G1 ok c1 --by human"
    And I run "gdd launch c1"
    And the file ".gdd/changes/c1/review.md" says:
      """
      ## How it works
      The parser keeps the old format and adds the new one beside it.

      ## Improvements
      - shorter names

      VERDICT: OK
      """
    When I run "gdd inbox c1"
    Then it succeeds
    And the output contains "The parser keeps the old format"
    And the output does not contain "shorter names"

  Scenario: A heading of another level or case still counts
    Given I run "gdd new-change c1 --title App --paths src/app.txt"
    And the change "c1" has the scenario "features/app.feature" on its branch
    And I am on the branch "change/c1"
    And I run "gdd gate G1 ok c1 --by human"
    And I run "gdd launch c1"
    And the file ".gdd/changes/c1/review.md" says:
      """
      ### how it works
      One cache per project, cleared when the rules change.

      VERDICT: OK
      """
    When I open the sitting of "c1"
    Then the sitting shows "One cache per project, cleared when the rules change."
    And the sitting does not show "the Reviewer did not explain the change"
